  Scope Management 
  - In-scope items 

The project will include email header and email user analysis. It will provide a risk analysis with a score rating as well as a small explanation on why it thinks it’s risky. It will detect keywords and grammatical errors commonly found in phishing emails.  
  - Out-of-scope items 

The project will not delete fake emails as well as executing any malware or applications a scam email may come with. It will also not block emails from fake accounts that are sending them 
  - Project assumptions and constraints 

You could assume that the project will be done on Spyder using Python. The emails used to determine if they are fake will all be crafted with AI or found online, so we don’t accidentally upload malware into the tester.  

Some constraints with this project will be that we may not find enough phishing emails to submit into the analyzer so we can perfect it. Another issue may be the limited database Python has when conducting the analysis. Lastly, the tool isn’t going to be 100% right all the time, so sometimes it may flag real emails as fake or miss things in phishing emails that would be spotted by a human.  

